# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Front Triage Agent (operations)

Watches Front conversations and drafts grounded replies as INTERNAL
comments — a human sends every customer-facing reply. Event-driven — no cron,
no servers to maintain. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Front rule ("Send to a webhook" — unsigned; the URL secret IS the auth)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/front-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/front-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output |
|---|---|---|
| New conversation | `triage` | ONE internal comment (draft reply + category); GitHub issue only for real bugs |
| New message on a tracked conversation | `respond` | Updated internal comment — or silence when a teammate already replied |

State lives on the orphan branch `front-agent-state` (`state/<conversation_id>.json`:
phase, last_message_at, issue_url). Every run re-fetches truth from Front's
API and diffs against it — webhook payloads are only doorbells. Agent comments
are prefixed `{{AGENT_MARKER}} — ` for humans, but loop protection is
STRUCTURAL: the agent writes COMMENTS, and the resolver counts only MESSAGES
(customer traffic + teammate replies) for recency, so its own output can never
ring its own doorbell. Recency is the message `created_at` — an epoch FLOAT,
compared numerically in jq, never in bash.

## Operating

- **Recover / backfill:** Actions → *Front Triage Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles recent open conversations + tracked ones; a conversation id (`cnv_…`) processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `CLAUDE_MODEL` in `scripts/front-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{CLAUDE_MODEL}}`).
- **Pause:** disable the rule(s) (Front → Settings → Rules) — no code change needed.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs FRONT_TOKEN exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/front-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=cnv_XXXX bash scripts/front-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Front writes are **internal comments only** — `note.sh` posts to the `/comments` endpoint, a stream Front never sends to customers, so the agent is structurally unable to reply; a human sends every reply.
- Never archives, assigns, or tags conversations — humans own the queue.
- Never escalates twice: the GitHub issue URL is saved in state (`issue_url`); follow-ups comment on that issue instead of opening a new one.
- No customer personal data (names, emails) in GitHub issues — describe, don't paste.
- Rule webhooks are unsigned — the relay authenticates by the secret URL path; rotate `WEBHOOK_SECRET` (and every rule's URL) if it ever leaks. Hardening path: Front's signed application webhooks, once you're willing to build a developer app.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only inside the disposable CI runner; local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call.
